              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<p>...in black and white\n</p><p>Susie is really white and black, Shay is definitely black and white.\n</p><p>In English, the phrase \"White and Black\" feels odd, wrong, an error. ....But for a dog that is more white than black using the phrase \"White and Black\" does actually convey useful extra information but \"black and white\" just reads/sounds better,\n</p><p>Interestingly (well I think it is interesting anyway), in Spanish the conventional order is the other way round \"blanco y negro\" so \"white and black\", and to say \"negro y blanco\" feels odd/wrong.\n</p>\nI dont usually post B&amp;W   pics but I see the November explore takeover is  B&amp;W themed ...so I have one to enter now!",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
